1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,490
x264 -crf 0: lossless?

2
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:16,500
RGB in. Is it RGB out, bit for bit?

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:23,770
25 frames, 320x180, RGB.

4
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:34,680
Two readers: frame md5, and PSNR.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:43,090
FFV1: 25 of 25 identical, psnr inf.

6
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:51,500
libx264rgb -crf 0: same, stored as RGB.

7
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,890
Stored as yuv444p, chosen quietly.

8
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:07,660
Back in RGB: 0 of 25 identical. psnr 54.6 dB.

9
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:18,270
Compared in yuv444p: 25 of 25 identical.

10
00:01:18,270 --> 00:01:30,400
The gap is the RGB to YUV conversion.

11
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:42,980
yuv420p: psnr 24.0 dB (6.1.1), 22.8 dB (8.1.2).

12
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:52,420
Exact in yuv420p, not in RGB.

13
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:59,630
Need RGB back? libx264rgb or FFV1.

14
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:08,040
Not tested: other codecs, real footage, hardware.
